<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominican Restoration War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1863–1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dominican Restoration War was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war fought from 1863 to 1865 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s reannexation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>. It began with the Grito de Capotillo on 16 August 1863, and the rebels set up a provisional government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, with leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregorio-luperon">Gregorio Luperón</a>. Disease and guerrilla attacks wore down the Spanish army, and Spain withdrew in 1865, restoring Dominican independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dominican-restoration-war.jpg" alt="Dominican Restoration War" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_de_la_isla_de_Santo_Domingo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
